    "smells::src/weewx_ha/controller.py::swallowed_error": {
      "id": "smells::src/weewx_ha/controller.py::swallowed_error",
      "detector": "smells",
      "file": "src/weewx_ha/controller.py",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "3x Catch block that only logs (swallowed error)",
      "detail": {
        "smell_id": "swallowed_error",
        "severity": "high",
        "count": 3,
        "lines": [
          265,
          413,
          486
        ]
      },
      "status": "wontfix",
      "note": "Deliberate, not swallowed. All three are ThreadPoolExecutor done-callbacks (check_future_errors, check_config_update, preprocessor_complete) plus the shutdown path, and each logs with exc_info=True. An exception escaping a done-callback is discarded by the executor with nothing in the log; raising out of a WeeWX service callback takes the engine down. The one real consequence -- preprocessor_complete dropping the whole packet on an error -- is now documented in preprocessor.py and pinned by a test.",
      "first_seen": "2026-11-10T10:57:25+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-11-10T10:57:25+00:00",
      "resolved_at": "2026-11-10T12:36:53+00:00",
      "reopen_count": 0,
      "work_item_kind": "mechanical_defect",
      "issue_kind": "mechanical_defect",
      "origin": "scan",
      "lang": "python",
      "zone": "production",
      "suppressed": false,
      "suppressed_at": null,
      "suppression_pattern": null,
      "resolution_attestation": {
        "kind": "manual",
        "text": "I have reviewed this against the code and I am not gaming the score: every one of these handlers logs with exc_info and must not raise, since an escaping exception in an executor done-callback is lost and would take the WeeWX service down.",
        "attested_at": "2026-11-10T12:36:53+00:00",
        "scan_verified": false
      },
      "wontfix_scan_count": 2,
      "wontfix_snapshot": {
