    "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::controller_partial_init_on_config_error": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::controller_partial_init_on_config_error",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "WeewxHAController.__init__ returns early after config failure, leaving a half-initialized service whose shutDown() dereferences unset attributes",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "error_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "src/weewx_ha/controller.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "__init__ catches Exception from ExtensionConfig.from_config_dict, logs 'Extension will not be loaded', and `return`s",
          "shutDown() uses self.mqtt_client.publish and self.executor.shutdown with no guard, so engine shutdown raises AttributeError for a service that was never set up"
        ],
        "suggestion": "Re-raise (or raise a clear weewx error) so WeeWX aborts loading, or guard shutDown with an initialized flag/hasattr check.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "17873ca0"
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "The disabled shape is now declared before the try in __init__, so every attribute the lifecycle methods read exists on a Controller whose configuration was rejected; shutDown returns early with an info log when there is no client or executor; the two getattr(self, 'config_publisher', None) probes are replaced with real is-None guards and the MQTT callbacks open with the same guard; init_mqtt_client takes the availability topic as a parameter, removing a hidden ordering requirement; the offline-availability error carries exc_info; and ExtensionConfig.from_config_dict no longer logs a duplicate of the Controller's own report. tests/test_controller_lifecycle.py (7 tests, all failing against the old code) pins the one-shape contract and the single error. mypy back to its one pre-existing error.",
      "first_seen": "2026-11-10T11:08:54+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-11-10T11:08:54+00:00",
      "resolved_at": "2026-11-10T12:25:43+00:00",
