    "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::locale_load_failures_swallowed_dead_checks": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::locale_load_failures_swallowed_dead_checks",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "Locale/YAML load failures are swallowed into {} while utils raises RuntimeError on unreachable None checks",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "error_consistency",
        "related_files": [
          "src/weewx_ha/locale_loader.py",
          "src/weewx_ha/utils.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "locale_loader catches FileNotFoundError/YAMLError on the base file, logs, and returns {} so a broken packaged file yields silently empty sensors/units/enums",
          "utils.get_enum_maps etc. raise RuntimeError('... failed to load') if the cache is None, but load_* never returns None, making the checks dead and the real failure mode silent"
        ],
        "suggestion": "Treat a missing/invalid base file as fatal (raise with original cause); keep fallback only for optional localized overlays; drop the dead None checks or make them meaningful.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "e297a66c"
      },
      "status": "wontfix",
      "note": "defer-to-followup-pr/error-contract - the proposed fix makes a missing or malformed packaged base YAML raise instead of degrading to {}, which turns a condition a WeeWX service currently tolerates into a hard startup failure of the whole weather station. That is a risk change, not a defect fix, and this cycle's split rule keeps only behaviour-correcting fixes in the bugfix PR. It needs its own PR where the new failure mode is the headline rather than a footnote under four unrelated bug fixes. The finding is NOT dropped: the contradiction it names is real - locale_loader.load_yaml returns {} on FileNotFoundError and yaml.YAMLError while the utils getters at lines 39-40, 47-48 and 55-56 advertise a RuntimeError that can therefore never fire - and the follow-up PR must settle it in one direction (raise for the packaged base, or delete the dead RuntimeError guards and document degradation as intended).",
      "first_seen": "2026-11-10T11:08:54+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-11-10T11:08:54+00:00",
      "resolved_at": "2026-11-10T11:42:10+00:00",
