    "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::loader_error_contract_conflict": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::loader_error_contract_conflict",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "load_yaml swallows missing/invalid base files and returns {}, while utils getters advertise a RuntimeError that can never fire",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "contract_coherence",
        "related_files": [
          "src/weewx_ha/locale_loader.py",
          "src/weewx_ha/utils.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "load_yaml: except FileNotFoundError / yaml.YAMLError -> logger.error(...); return {} (verified for a nonexistent file).",
          "utils.get_enum_maps/_get_unit_metadata_dict/get_sensors_yaml: 'if _X is None: raise RuntimeError(... failed to load)' is dead code after _ensure_loaded(), since load_* never returns None.",
          "A packaged-resource failure therefore surfaces later as a KeyError (e.g. get_enum_maps()['cardinal_directions'] in degrees_to_cardinal) instead of a clear load error.",
          "load_enums/load_units annotate precise value types but return load_yaml's dict[str, Any]."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Pick one error contract: let load_yaml raise for the packaged base file (it is a packaging error, not a runtime condition) and drop the dead None checks, or make the getters validate non-empty results and raise.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "afd54433"
      },
      "status": "wontfix",
      "note": "defer-to-followup-pr/error-contract - the proposed fix makes a missing or malformed packaged base YAML raise instead of degrading to {}, which turns a condition a WeeWX service currently tolerates into a hard startup failure of the whole weather station. That is a risk change, not a defect fix, and this cycle's split rule keeps only behaviour-correcting fixes in the bugfix PR. It needs its own PR where the new failure mode is the headline rather than a footnote under four unrelated bug fixes. The finding is NOT dropped: the contradiction it names is real - locale_loader.load_yaml returns {} on FileNotFoundError and yaml.YAMLError while the utils getters at lines 39-40, 47-48 and 55-56 advertise a RuntimeError that can therefore never fire - and the follow-up PR must settle it in one direction (raise for the packaged base, or delete the dead RuntimeError guards and document degradation as intended).",
      "first_seen": "2026-11-10T11:08:54+00:00",
      "last_seen": "2026-11-10T11:08:54+00:00",
      "resolved_at": "2026-11-10T11:42:10+00:00",
      "reopen_count": 0,
