    "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::controller_partial_construction": {
      "id": "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::controller_partial_construction",
      "detector": "review",
      "file": ".",
      "tier": 2,
      "confidence": "medium",
      "summary": "Controller.__init__ 'will not be loaded' path returns normally, leaving a half-initialised service whose shutDown raises AttributeError",
      "detail": {
        "holistic": true,
        "dimension": "contract_coherence",
        "related_files": [
          "src/weewx_ha/controller.py"
        ],
        "evidence": [
          "On config failure __init__ logs 'Extension will not be loaded' and returns; engine still holds the object and calls shutDown.",
          "Verified: Controller.__new__(Controller).shutDown() raises AttributeError: no attribute 'mqtt_client' (swallowed only by StdEngine.shutDown's bare except).",
          "on_mqtt_connect/on_mqtt_message guard with getattr(self, 'config_publisher', None) to cope with the same partially-built state."
        ],
        "suggestion": "Either re-raise so WeeWX actually does not load the service, or initialise all attributes (mqtt_client/executor = None) up front and make shutDown a no-op when not started.",
        "reasoning": "",
        "summary_hash": "f210c27a"
      },
      "status": "fixed",
      "note": "The disabled shape is now declared before the try in __init__, so every attribute the lifecycle methods read exists on a Controller whose configuration was rejected; shutDown returns early with an info log when there is no client or executor; the two getattr(self, 'config_publisher', None) probes are replaced with real is-None guards and the MQTT callbacks open with the same guard; init_mqtt_client takes the availability topic as a parameter, removing a hidden ordering requirement; the offline-availability error carries exc_info; and ExtensionConfig.from_config_dict no longer logs a duplicate of the Controller's own report. tests/test_controller_lifecycle.py (7 tests, all failing against the old code) pins the one-shape contract and the single error. mypy back to its one pre-existing error.",
