        "text": "I have actually The disabled shape is now declared before the try in __init__, so every attribute the lifecycle methods read exists on a Controller whose configuration was rejected; shutDown returns early with an info log when there is no client or executor; the two getattr(self, 'config_publisher', None) probes are replaced with real is-None guards and the MQTT callbacks open with the same guard; init_mqtt_client takes the availability topic as a parameter, removing a hidden ordering requirement; the offline-availability error carries exc_info; and ExtensionConfig.from_config_dict no longer logs a duplicate of the Controller's own report. tests/test_controller_lifecycle.py (7 tests, all failing against the old code) pins the one-shape contract and the single error. mypy back to its one pre-existing error. and I am not gaming the score.",
